---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Word Seeker"
  description="Privacy Policy for the Word Seeker application developed by developedbyjacob."
>
  <section class="pt-28 pb-16 md:pt-32 md:pb-24">
    <div class="container-app max-w-3xl">
      <a
        href="/"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 hover:text-accent-600 dark:hover:text-accent-400 transition-colors mb-8"
      >
        <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" />
        </svg>
        Back to portfolio
      </a>

      <span class="text-accent-600 dark:text-accent-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-widest uppercase notranslate">
        Legal
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mt-2 mb-4">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-2">
        <span class="notranslate">Word Seeker</span>
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-500 notranslate">
        Last updated: July 12, 2026
      </p>

      <div class="prose-policy mt-10 space-y-8 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy explains how <span class="notranslate">developedbyjacob</span>
          handles information related to the use of the
          <span class="notranslate">Word Seeker</span> application, hereinafter the "Application".
        </p>
        <p>By using the Application, the user accepts the practices described in this Privacy Policy.</p>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">1. Application controller</h2>
          <p>Developer: <span class="notranslate">developedbyjacob</span></p>
          <p>Contact email: <a href="mailto:kiktruedeveloper@gmail.com" class="text-accent-700 dark:text-accent-400 hover:underline notranslate">kiktruedeveloper@gmail.com</a></p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">2. Information stored in the Application</h2>
          <p>The Application is a word search puzzle game that allows users to find hidden words across different categories and difficulties. To provide these features, the Application may store the following information locally on the device:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-1">
            <li>Game progress: the grid, words placed, words already found, remaining hints, and elapsed time of a game in progress.</li>
            <li>Game statistics: games played, games won, best time, and total words found, grouped by difficulty level (Easy, Medium, Hard).</li>
            <li>Win streak counter.</li>
            <li>User preferences: selected language for word lists and interface, dark theme setting, and sound effects setting.</li>
            <li>Premium (ad-free) purchase status.</li>
            <li>Interstitial ad display counter.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">This information is stored locally on the user's device and is not sent to servers operated by the developer. The developer cannot access, view, or retrieve the game data saved by the user.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">3. Language selection</h2>
          <p>The Application allows users to select a preferred language for the word lists used in puzzles and for the user interface. By default, the Application uses the language of the device. If the user manually selects a different language, this preference is stored locally on the device.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">Changing the language deletes any game in progress, as word lists are language-dependent. This deletion happens exclusively on the device.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">4. Advertising through Google AdMob</h2>
          <p>The Application displays banner, interstitial, and rewarded advertisements through <span class="notranslate">Google AdMob</span>, a service provided by Google. Rewarded advertisements allow users to obtain additional hints by watching a video ad.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">The Google Mobile Ads SDK may automatically collect and share certain information, such as:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-1">
            <li>IP address, which may be used to estimate the device's general location.</li>
            <li>Device or advertising identifiers, such as the Android Advertising ID or App Set ID.</li>
            <li>Information about interactions with the Application and advertisements (impressions, clicks, video views).</li>
            <li>Diagnostic and performance information, such as errors, startup times, or SDK operation.</li>
            <li>Technical information about the device, operating system, and Application.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">Google may use this information to show advertisements, measure their performance, perform analytics, limit their frequency, and prevent fraud or misuse. Depending on the user's location, settings, and consent, advertisements may be personalized or non-personalized.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">Information processed by Google is subject to Google's terms and privacy policies. The user can view and change advertising preferences in the privacy and advertising settings of their Google account or Android device.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">Information related to game progress, statistics, and user preferences is not deliberately sent to Google AdMob to personalize advertisements.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">5. Advertising consent</h2>
          <p>In territories where legally required, the Application may display a consent message through Google's User Messaging Platform (UMP) allowing the user to manage their privacy and advertising preferences.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">The user may accept, reject, or modify certain options related to the use of data for personalized advertising, according to the options available in Google's consent message.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">Withdrawing consent does not necessarily prevent advertisements from being shown, but they may be non-personalized or subject to more limited data processing.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">6. In-app purchases</h2>
          <p>The Application offers a one-time in-app purchase to remove advertisements. This purchase is processed through <span class="notranslate">Google Play Billing</span>. The developer does not receive or store payment card details or banking information.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">Purchase history and transaction records are managed by Google and are subject to Google's privacy policies. The developer only stores a local flag indicating whether the user has purchased the ad-free experience.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">7. Purpose of processing</h2>
          <p>The information described in this Policy is used to:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-1">
            <li>Provide the core word search gameplay features.</li>
            <li>Save and resume games in progress.</li>
            <li>Track statistics and win streaks per difficulty level.</li>
            <li>Apply user preferences (language, theme, sound).</li>
            <li>Display and measure advertisements through Google AdMob.</li>
            <li>Deliver rewarded advertisements in exchange for hints.</li>
            <li>Manage the ad-free purchase through Google Play Billing.</li>
            <li>Maintain the security, stability, and operation of the Application.</li>
            <li>Prevent fraud and misuse related to advertising.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">Game data and statistics are not sold or used by the developer for external commercial purposes.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">8. Data retention and deletion</h2>
          <p>Locally stored game data remains on the device until the user:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-1">
            <li>Completes a game (game data is cleared upon completion).</li>
            <li>Exits and chooses not to save the game in progress.</li>
            <li>Clears the Application's data in Android settings.</li>
            <li>Uninstalls the Application.</li>
            <li>Uses any deletion feature available within the Application.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">Because the developer does not receive or store this data on its own servers, it cannot delete it remotely or recover it after it has been deleted. Data processed by Google AdMob is retained according to the policies and periods established by Google.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">9. Security</h2>
          <p>The Application uses the storage and security mechanisms provided by Android. However, no electronic system can guarantee absolute security. Users are advised to protect their device with a password, PIN, pattern, fingerprint, or another locking method.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">Data transmitted by the Google Mobile Ads SDK and Google Play Billing is sent over encrypted connections.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">10. Children</h2>
          <p>The Application is not specifically designed for children and does not knowingly seek to collect personal information from minors. Google AdMob is configured to serve ads appropriate for all audiences.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">If a parent or guardian believes that a minor has improperly provided personal information, they may contact the developer using the email address indicated in this Policy.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">11. Third-party services</h2>
          <p>The Application may interact with external services, mainly:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-1">
            <li>Google AdMob (advertising).</li>
            <li>Google Play Billing (in-app purchases).</li>
            <li>Google User Messaging Platform (consent management).</li>
            <li>Google Play (sharing the app or leaving a rating).</li>
            <li>Android system services for storage and sharing.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">Processing performed by these services is governed by their own privacy policies and terms of use.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">12. User rights and control</h2>
          <p>The user retains control over game data stored on their device and can view, modify, or delete it from the Application or the Android system settings.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">The user can also:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-1">
            <li>Reset or delete the advertising identifier in the device's privacy settings.</li>
            <li>Manage Google advertising and privacy preferences.</li>
            <li>Clear the Application's data in Android settings.</li>
            <li>Uninstall the Application.</li>
            <li>Change the app language at any time from the Settings screen.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">For any privacy-related questions, the user can contact the developer at <a href="mailto:kiktruedeveloper@gmail.com" class="text-accent-700 dark:text-accent-400 hover:underline notranslate">kiktruedeveloper@gmail.com</a>.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">13. Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
          <p>This Privacy Policy may be updated when new features, external services, or legal changes are introduced. The date of the last update will appear at the beginning of the document. Users are advised to review this Policy periodically to learn about any changes.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">14. Contact</h2>
          <p>For questions, requests, or concerns related to this Privacy Policy, you can use the following email address:</p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            <a href="mailto:kiktruedeveloper@gmail.com" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-accent-700 dark:text-accent-400 hover:underline font-medium notranslate">
              <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3 8l7.89 5.26a2 2 0 002.22 0L21 8M5 19h14a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2z" />
              </svg>
              kiktruedeveloper@gmail.com
            </a>
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
